b5c0b95..1142306 preserves the reparam driver's output: 1142306 is e776c04 (code-identical to 5faaa15, covered by b5c0b95-5faaa15) plus the per-call BLAS thread pin, and the 23 paired driver runs are identical outside timing and provenance. The pin runs on every driver call, but at the driver's own BLAS count, so this record shows the wrapper changes no output at one BLAS thread; it does not measure a caller that starts with more threads, whose draws change by design.

1142306 (snag openblas-threads-2f1bf9e9, design decision 0vb5vs6) adds src/blas_threads.jl, included from src/WarmupHMC.jl, and a `blas_threads` keyword (default 1, `nothing` = untouched) on adaptive_warmup_mcmc (both methods), resume_warmup_mcmc (both methods), completion_warmup_mcmc, cooperative_warmup_mcmc, every stream_mcmc method and fixed_kernel_nuts_step. Each body runs inside `_with_blas_threads(blas_threads)`, which records BLAS.get_num_threads(), sets the requested count only when it differs, and restores the recorded count when the last active call leaves. src/kwarg_validation.jl adds `:blas_threads` to the accepted sets. No sampler arithmetic changes. common.jl calls BLAS.set_num_threads(1) at load, so in the driver the pin finds 1 and sets nothing; every `adaptive_warmup_mcmc` call the driver makes still passes through it.

Evidence: docs/benchmark/run_reparam_benchmark.jl with WHMC_BENCH_TARGETS=funnel,eight_schools-eight_schools_centered,seeds_data-seeds_centered_model,radon_mn-radon_partially_pooled_centered,radon_mn-radon_variable_intercept_centered, WHMC_BENCH_SEEDS=1 and WHMC_BENCH_DRAWS=1000 (WHMC_BENCH_AD unset): 23 runs per side, 0 failed. after/ was run on gordito on 2026-10-27 with Julia 1.10.12 in a clean clone at 1142306, with docs/benchmark developed against that clone and Treebars at the kb-extdep mirror tip (98344e0, which carries 4c09a18). before/ is the same b5c0b95 run as b5c0b95-5faaa15/before/ and b5c0b95-249f72d/before/ (same targets, seeds and draws; byte-identical files). before/ and after/ also keep the driver's gradient_overhead.json.

What this record does not show: behaviour at more than one BLAS thread (covered by test/blas_threads.jl, which reads the count inside the target's gradient for every entry point), and the completion, cooperative and streaming samplers, which no driver arm calls. For the other sampler harnesses (BRM inventory and catalogue, linear restart, nonlinear weighting, adaptive centering at fixed c, sampler comparison) the claim rests on the same argument: each sets BLAS to one thread at load, so the pin sets nothing there either.
